menu: Return focus to the trigger before running an item

- PopupMenu dismisses itself before it runs the chosen item, so a dialog
  opened by the item records the menu's trigger as its opener, not the
  menu that is about to be released. Actions keep their dispatch path.
- A dropdown tracks one stable focus handle on its trigger, and dismissal
  returns there even when a pointer opened the menu while another control
  had focus.
- DropdownMenuPopover::open controls visibility, and
  DropdownButton::menu_trigger customizes the menu half of a split button.

Remove when upstream restores menu focus this way.

